 Yes! With PWAs, updates happen automatically (with a small catch). When users visit your PWA, the browser checks for updates in the background. Next time they open it, boom - new version. No app store, no "Update" button, no version 2.3.5 nonsense.

**The catch**: You need a simple service worker update strategy:

```javascript
// In your service worker
self.addEventListener('activate', event => {
  // Clear old caches, force new content
  event.waitUntil(
    caches.keys().then(cacheNames => {
      return Promise.all(
        cacheNames.filter(cacheName => cacheName !== 'v2')
          .map(cacheName => caches.delete(cacheName))
      );
    })
  );
});
```

